      "text": [
        ": قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ مَيِّتٌ قُطِعَ رَأْسُهُ قَالَ \"عَلَيْهِ اَلدِّيَةُ\" قُلْتُ فَمَنْ يَأْخُذُ دِيَتَهُ قَالَ \"اَلْإِمَامُ هَذَا لِلَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ إِنْ قُطِعَتْ يَمِينُهُ أَوْ شَيْءٌ مِنْ جَوَارِحِهِ فَعَلَيْهِ اَلْأَرْشُ لِلْإِمَامِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5358 - It is narrated from Abu Jamilah, from Ishaq ibn Ammar, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a deceased person whose head was cut off.\nImam (as) said: \"The blood money is upon the one who did it.\"\nI asked: \"Who receives his blood money?\"\nImam (as) said: \"The Imam, for this belongs to Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic. And if his right hand or any of his limbs is cut off, the compensation (Al-arsh) is also due to the Imam.\""
        ]
      }
